To make the browser use an HTTP proxy, you can configure it using the `new_browser_context` method with the `proxy` option. Set the `server` parameter to your proxy URL and optionally provide `username` and `password` if required. Here's an example:

```python
browser_context = playwright.chromium.launch().new_browser_context(
    proxy={
        "server": "http://10.0.0.1:1080",
        "username": "user",
        "password": "pass"
    }
)
```
